ok - fm-teardown --retire-record: drops every state record of a superseded task and nothing of the current holder's, the working copy, or the pool
ok - fm-teardown --retire-record --dry-run: prints the verdict and the records it would drop, and changes nothing
ok - fm-teardown --retire-record --dry-run: scans for armed checks over what completing a pending receipt would leave, so its verdict matches the real run's in both directions
ok - fm-teardown --retire-record: refuses a record the pool still leases to it, and the lease proves the older claimant re-leased
ok - fm-teardown --retire-record: a claim is unproven unless the pool's lease confirms it or another record's claim on the same path explains it, and the leased record is refused as the holder
